{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/802420-feedback-2nd-edition-non-affinity-shadow-gifts-moon-gifts-and-wolf-facets-xp-costs","id":802420,"title":"[FEEDBACK 2nd Edition] Non-Affinity Shadow Gifts, Moon Gifts and Wolf Facets xp costs","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-06T16:16:59-08:00","id":802420,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon3.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> [FEEDBACK 2nd Edition] Non-Affinity Shadow Gifts, Moon Gifts and Wolf Facets xp costs","content":"I've read WtF 2nd Edition about twice now and I'm currently storytelling a WtF campaing for 2 months.I do not agree with the experience costs of unlocking moon gifts, shadow gifts and also the cost of buying Wolf Gift Facets. Here is my reasoning after considering the costs:<br /> <br /> <b>1 - Unlocking a new 'line&quot; of moon gifts should cost 3 points.</b> The uratha should be considered to have affinity with them, since its their moon. When you increase your auspice renown, the system gives the character a moon facet along with a new gift from increasing any renown. This makes their moon gift to look like having a lot of &quot;affinity&quot;both mechanicaly and conceptualy. After the new line of auspice gift is unlocked, then each facet would cost 2 points as normal (and bought in order up to renown rating).<br /> <b>2 - Unlocking a Non-Affiniy Shadow Gift should cost 4 points instead of 5.</b> Vampires pay 4 points to buy a non-clan discipline and also Cru\u00e1c and non-chosen mistery of Coils of The Dragon. It seems to me that only Primal Urge (as much as any &quot;Supernatural Potency&quot; trait) should cost 5 points, which is very expensive considering the experience system.<br /> <b>3 - Wolf Gift Facets should cost 2 points each.</b> I've read all gifts of the core book and when I saw that wolf facets would already be unlocked (which makes a lot of sense) and cost 1 point each, I've read them in hope of finding they'd be weaker than shadow gift facets, but they aren't. The &quot;2 points per facet&quot; system of unlocked gifts works well with the system and I think the fact that every werewolf has open access to buy them literaly at any time they have the experience (whithout hunting or negotiating with a spirit, for example) makes them &quot;free enough&quot;. Mind that players will have access to experience on a one-at-time basis and this &quot;liberty&quot; of buying wolf facets will make players (its making mine, lol) too eager to buy them, specialy when they find out that they're as good as the shadow ones. They can get two (from renown they have) for two experiences instead of one shadow gift. The argument is somewhat like what I said about Primal Urge above - only merits and skill specialties should cost 1 point dot/each, given their cost/benefit comparisons. What will happen with these costs is that, when the players buy a new renown dot, they'll go only for shadow gifts (if they can, which is not difficult) for that renown instead of getting a wolf gift because the later are so incredibly cheap and they can buy those at any time with one experience each.<br /> <br /> I'm applying these rules on my game because I think it makes everything more balanced and also because I don't want my werewolves to have all the wolf gits they can get. Or was that was the intended way the way that the developers wanted? Of course, as the storyteller I can easily hold their &quot;metagamic&quot; minds, but I also think customization should always be balanced so the choices have more incentive based on fairness.<br /> <br /> Too bad the book is already printed. If anyone had the same feeling when they played or read the gift costs, these suggestions above may work as a house rule.<br /> <br /> <i>PS: I loved WtF 2nd Edition, its close to perfect. I recommend it to anyone and, yes, it has gotten better than 1st Edition (imo). I've had many complaints about 1st edition nWoD books (rule-wise only) but the way Onyx is handling CofD (2nd Edition) is being wonderful. This is actualy the only thing I found wrong (again, imo) on WtF 2nd Edition.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10798-kitsune-sensei","name":"Kitsune Sensei","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10798_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-06T16:37:55-08:00","id":802436,"title":"","content":"Cool. Golden rule says, in your table stuff can cost as much XP as you want. In my table, players engaging in the Siskur Dah episodically + the benefits of Song in your Heart means they're practically doubling their earned beats, not to mention the ones earned from resolving the shitload of beneficial conditions gathered from those exceptional successes.<br /> <br /> Any Uratha that performs the Sacred Hunt <b><i>religiously </i></b>is a force to be reckoned with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-06T16:53:45-08:00","id":802453,"title":"","content":"I don't necessarily disagree with anything you've said here, though neither do I think it's egregious enough to bother houseruling anything (for me anyway).<br /> <br /> You can go ahead and houserule it in any game you're running and I doubt there would be any complaints.<br /> <br /> I will say, though, that I don't think it's fair to compare the Werewolf gift costs to the Vampire Discipline costs.<br /> <br /> It costs 5 to unlock a new non-affinity gift, but only 2xp each to earn the rest of its Facets, or 3xp each (via renown). Meaning acquiring all the facets of a non-affinity gift can cost as little as 13 xp, and 17xp at the most. Compared with 19-20 for an unfavored Discipline (depending on whether or not you started with the first dot). That seems like a deal to me. It basically evens out if you purchase a single Facet after unlocking the Gift.<br /> <br /> Not to mention that werewolf gifts scale entirely differently, and <i>generally</i> more efficiently, at the cost of having to perform feats to earn the increases. (A werewolf with Slaughterer and Primal Strength, for example, is doing the rough equivalent of scaling a dot of Vigor everytime he earns Purity, all the while getting extra Facets for his trouble).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-06T17:14:58-08:00","id":802467,"title":"","content":"The reason that unlocking a Shadow Gift is worth 5xp is because unlocking a Facet costs 2xp - unlocking a Gift and all the Facets costs 15xp, which is the same amount a Vampire pays for all 5 dots of one of their in-Clan Disciplines. Think of it less as &quot;oh, I'm buying an out of clan Discipline here&quot; and more &quot;I am turning an out-of-clan Discipline into an in-Clan discipline.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-06T19:03:56-08:00","id":802547,"title":"","content":"It's worth keeping in mind that when you unlock a Shadow gift you also buy a facet with it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Werewolf the Forsaken Second Edition</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unlocking a Shadow Gift costs 5 Experiences, or 3 if it is favored by auspice or tribe. Once it is acquired, the Uratha gains a single Facet within that Gift immediately.</div> </div> </div> </div>So the true cost is like 1 Experience to unlock an Affinity gift, 3 for a non-Affinity or Moon gift.<br /> <br /> I also really disagree about Wolf Gifts not being less powerful than Shadow Gifts, but no one's going to settle that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 01-06-2016, 10:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T07:17:54-08:00","id":804435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kitsune Sensei</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/802420-feedback-2nd-edition-non-affinity-shadow-gifts-moon-gifts-and-wolf-facets-xp-costs#post802420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>1 - Unlocking a new 'line&quot; of moon gifts should cost 3 points.</b></div> </div> </div> </div> Moon Gifts are powerful new capabilities to unlock. Think of it this way; 5 Experiences *is* a Moon Gift at affinity discount; a lack of affinity means you can't buy it at all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>2 - Unlocking a Non-Affiniy Shadow Gift should cost 4 points instead of 5.</b> </div> </div> </div> Don't worry about what vampires pay for their powers - inasmuch as we considered any other supernatural game-line's capabilities and XP costs, it's already factored in to how we approached the overall costing of Gifts (which is a complex interaction of Gifts, Facet costs and Renown).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>3 - Wolf Gift Facets should cost 2 points each.</b> </div> </div> </div> Wolf Facets being cheaper was very much a specific design decision. They're intended to be minor powers closely-aligned with the werewolf concept. Players being able to cheaply acquire the Wolf Facets they want is entirely the system working as intended. In practice, in playtesting, players did not shirk Shadow Gifts to only buy Wolf Facets. They all do different things, Wolf Facets tend to be more minor in impact than Shadow Facets, and Wolf Facets simply don't replace Shadow Facets in terms of the capabilities that the latter offer.<br /> <br /> Players generally choosing to go for Shadow Facets rather than Wolf Facets with the free one from a Renown dot is also the system working just fine, not a bug.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Too bad the book is already printed. </div> </div> </div> I'll be honest - if the book hadn't yet been printed and I was given the chance to make further amendments to the Gifts system, there are a few things I would tweak or amend but I wouldn't change any of the Experience costs involved. Post-release play has only made me feel happier with the current XP costs we attached.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}